# Force LF line endings for all text files, regardless of each contributor's
# local core.autocrlf setting. Without this, a Windows checkout can silently
# convert LF -> CRLF on disk, which changes the exact byte content of a file
# — and drizzle-kit hashes migration files by raw content to decide whether
# they've already been applied. A CRLF-converted migration file hashes
# differently than the LF version committed to the repo, so `drizzle-kit
# migrate` never recognizes it as already-run and silently fails instead of
# reporting a clear error (a real upstream bug — see git history/session
# notes around the migration 0006-0009 debugging).
* text=auto eol=lf
